<.section_heading>
  {dgettext("landing", "Your data stays with you. Period.")}
</.section_heading>
<ul class="space-y-2 text-sm">
  <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
    <Icons.icon_checkmark class="w-4 h-4 shrink-0 mt-0.5" />
    <span>
      {dgettext("landing", "Messages stored on")}
      <strong>your</strong> {dgettext("landing", "server, never leave")}
    </span>
  </li>
  <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
    <Icons.icon_checkmark class="w-4 h-4 shrink-0 mt-0.5" />
    <span>
      {dgettext(
        "landing",
        "Private calls go direct P2P; channel conferences stay on your infrastructure"
      )}
    </span>
  </li>
  <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
    <Icons.icon_checkmark class="w-4 h-4 shrink-0 mt-0.5" />
    <span>{dgettext("landing", "Your data stays in your database, period")}</span>
  </li>
  <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
    <Icons.icon_checkmark class="w-4 h-4 shrink-0 mt-0.5" />
    <span>{dgettext("landing", "Open source — verify yourself")}</span>
  </li>
  <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
    <Icons.icon_checkmark class="w-4 h-4 shrink-0 mt-0.5" />
    <span>
      {dgettext("landing", "You own the server — nobody can shut you down")}
    </span>
  </li>
  <li class="flex items-start gap-2">
    <Icons.icon_checkmark class="w-4 h-4 shrink-0 mt-0.5" />
    <span>
      {dgettext("landing", "Your server operator controls message access and retention")}
    </span>
  </li>
</ul>
<h3 class="text-sm font-bold mt-4 mb-2">
  {dgettext("landing", "The one cookie that is not a login")}
</h3>
<p class="text-sm">
  {dgettext(
    "landing",
    "Your browser is given a random name so the server can tell your phone from your desktop. It identifies a browser, never a person: nothing is stored against it but which channels that screen had open and where in them you had read to, and a different browser on the same machine gets a different one. It follows you nowhere, because it only exists on this server."
  )}
</p>
<h3 class="text-sm font-bold mt-4 mb-2">
  {dgettext("landing", "The one thing that does leave: push notifications")}
</h3>
<p class="text-sm">
  {dgettext(
    "landing",
    "If you switch on notifications for when the chat is closed, your browser gives the server an address at its vendor's push service — Google's, Mozilla's or Apple's — and the server sends a notification there. What it sends is encrypted for your browser alone: the push service carries an address and a block of ciphertext, and can read neither the conversation nor the message."
  )}
</p>
<p class="text-sm mt-2">
  {dgettext(
    "landing",
    "It is off until you turn it on, it is per device, and the same switch in the Sounds window turns it off again. A self-hosted server with no VAPID key pair does not have the feature at all."
  )}
</p>
